  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-03-26T17:27:35.086Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "This is going to be a bit longer since I have a lot on my mind so bear with me.\n\nI started out on this Game around November 2017, the Knuckles Hype was more or less still going.\nI started out as what you would call a \"Desktop Pleb\" the only control I had was my XBOX Controller and using it to pick up stuff, aim, look around, you know the drill. After a few days of browsing around I found out I could use my Phone to atleast have the 3D Vision of course not in the Quality of Oculus, but I could have a taste of how it would feel to be actually able to atleast look around, it was amazing for me, and I decided to grab a mixed reality and later on trade it in for an oculus. I enjoyed my Time, not needing a VPN or a Hardware ID Spoofer to be safe, until shit started to hit the fan for the first time, most people probably remember the big Avatar leakage, with thousands of peoples work being on one world that got stolen, after that we got the option to set our work to private, so even with the Avatar ID being stolen the stuff wouldn't be able to be set on a world. But it wasn't enough, people started to cause more mischief, disconnect exploits, crashers, malicious stuff was all over the place like a forest fire it spread across the game. And it looked like nothing could stop it. I dont know why people get a boner from hacking in a social game, but that is not the point where I am getting at, after a while Devs kept patching out security holes atleast for a while, over the month, until the people said: \"Hey we need more security, our stuff is still being stolen.\" so what did the Devs decided on? On a Avatar Performance System, thats what we got, for those little Streamers, that don't care about this game or the content or the creators of the content, what they care about is just clicks and views, and if they dont lose the 3FPS out of their 90FPS, that was the first blow dealt against the community that enjoys the game for socializing, making friends, creating content and avatars, and even worlds sharing their Avatars and Animations alike. I know that there are people that like not really optimize their work at all, but the restrictions are just not really that well balanced. Now after a few month we got the Communitylabs another Feature that I welcome, because it gives Content Creators more Playground, but it seems it was also on the cost of an actual fix for the Security Flaws, and on top of that people found a way to grab your IP, a very personal information in my opinion, to cause more mischief, people made an uproar on canny, asking for explaination why this is a thing, all we got was an answer like \"Get a VPN if you dont feel safe.\" what kind of an Answer is that? You tell your players to install Extra Software to be safe in your environment, that you are responsible for? After that I thought, okay maybe they will work on something to actually get the Game safe, since leakage of such data is troublesome with certain lawsuits, and what do we get? A new Notification System. I don't know who thought this was a top priority on the Devs Side, but the old thing was still working fine, it would probably haven't hurt to focus on Security first, and then do the other planned stuff, but no, we definitly needed that Notification System. Player counts are decreasing slowly in Public, why? Because you don't feel safe any more in any kind of Instance with Strangers, without having the fear of something getting ripped or sniffed out (IPs, HWID etc.)\nAt this point, it just looks like those \"Security and Safety Hotfixes\" are just for the Hackers to be safe not to be banned instead of the actual Players. This Game was so much enjoyable back then, but now its just people battling each other with DDOS, Crashes and other shit.\n\nTL;DR: We want to enjoy this Game as much as possible, but I fear with the current \"security\" we will just be forced to keep sitting in Private Instances",
